   "text": "I read the molecule as a VHL-based degrader (PROTAC): a VHL ligand joined through a spiro linker to a bicyclic aminopyridazine\u2013phenol group. The SMILES below was assembled region by region from the drawing.\n\n**Regions, left to right**\n- **VHL ligand:** a 4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)benzylamide of (2S,4R)-4-hydroxyproline. The proline nitrogen is acylated by an L-tert-leucine, whose NH is acylated in turn. I matched the stereocentres to the standard VH032 ligand.\n- **Spiro linker:** the tert-leucine NH is acylated by a carboxamide on C7 of a spiro[3.5]nonane. C2 of the cyclobutane carries the piperidine nitrogen. The C7 carbonyl is wedged and the C2\u2013N bond is hashed.\n- **Piperidine to pyrimidine:** the piperidine's 4-position is bonded to C5 of a pyrimidine.\n- **Bicyclic amine:** pyrimidine C2 is bonded to N8 of a 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane. Its N3 is bonded to the pyridazine. No stereo is drawn for this bicycle.\n- **Pyridazine and phenol:** the pyridazine carries an NH2 next to the ring nitrogen and a 2-hydroxyphenyl group.\n\n**Spiro stereochemistry**\nThis part is the least certain. The two spiro stereocentres were assigned from the flat drawing by reading the wedge and the hash independently. I then converted each to SMILES chirality labels by hand.\n\nSMILES: Cc1ncsc1-c1ccc(CNC(=O)[C@@H]2C[C@@H](O)CN2C(=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)[C@@H]3CCC4(CC3)C[C@@H](C4)N3CCC(CC3)c3cnc(nc3)N3C5CCC3CN(C5)c3cc(nnc3N)-c3ccccc3O)C(C)(C)C)cc1"
